<td id="S5.T4.6.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.45pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S5.T4.6.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-bg-color:#F0F0F0;">   1.481 <span id="S5.T4.6.1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">(+0.30)</span>   </span></td>
<td id="S5.T4.6.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.45pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S5.T4.6.1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-bg-color:#F0F0F0;">   1.26<math id="S5.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#F0F0F0;" mathbackground="#F0F0F0">×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>   </span></td>
<td id="S5.T4.6.1.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.45pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S5.T4.6.1.4.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-bg-color:#F0F0F0;">   26.41 <span id="S5.T4.6.1.4.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">(+0.02)</span>   </span></td>
<td id="S5.T4.6.1.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.45pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S5.T4.6.1.4.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-bg-color:#F0F0F0;">   ✓   </span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T4.6.1.5" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F0F0F0;">
<th id="S5.T4.6.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb" style="padding:-0.45pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S5.T4.6.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-bg-color:#F0F0F0;">   <span id="S5.T4.6.1.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Prism-<math id="S5.T4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#F0F0F0;" mathbackground="#F0F0F0" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>V</span>   </span></th>
<td id="S5.T4.6.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:-0.45pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S5.T4.6.1.5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-bg-color:#F0F0F0;">   1.502 <span id="S5.T4.6.1.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">(+0.32)</span>   </span></td>
<td id="S5.T4.6.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:-0.45pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S5.T4.6.1.5.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-bg-color:#F0F0F0;">   1.26<math id="S5.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#F0F0F0;" mathbackground="#F0F0F0">×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>   </span></td>
<td id="S5.T4.6.1.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:-0.45pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S5.T4.6.1.5.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-bg-color:#F0F0F0;">   26.43 <span id="S5.T4.6.1.5.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">(+0.04)</span>   </span></td>
<td id="S5.T4.6.1.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:-0.45pt 20.0pt;"><span id="S5.T4.6.1.5.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-bg-color:#F0F0F0;">   ✓   </span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Table <a href="#S5.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 5.4 Efficiency analysis ‣ 5 Results ‣ Prism-Δ: Differential Subspace Steering for Prompt Highlighting in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, SEKA adds negligible overhead (+0.01 s, +0.04 GB) over the original model. <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Prism-<math id="S5.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math></span> adds +0.30 s latency (1.26<math id="S5.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>) due to the per-head softplus weight computation and weighted projection, with negligible additional memory (+0.02 GB). <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Prism-<math id="S5.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math>V</span> adds a further +0.02 s for Value editing. Both variants remain fully compatible with FlashAttention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dao et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dao, 2023</a>)</cite>. For comparison, PASTA adds +1.03 s and +23.12 GB, and SPA adds +5.32 s <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2026</a>)</cite>, placing <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Prism-<math id="S5.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math></span> in between SEKA and these heavier alternatives.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Analysis</h2>

